{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 28,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.087,
            0.252,
            0.106
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Page No. 154"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.118,
            0.299,
            0.136
          ],
          "content": "？ **Figure it out**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.147,
            0.883,
            0.205
          ],
          "content": "**1. We checked by construction that there are no triangles having sidelengths 3 cm, 4 cm and 8 cm; and 2 cm, 3 cm and 6 cm. Check if you could have found this without trying to construct the triangle.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.206,
            0.878,
            0.265
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** Here sum of the two sides (i.e 3 cm and 4 cm) is less than the third side (i.e 8 cm). Similarly for sides of lengths 2cm, 3cm and 6cm, 2 + 3 < 6. So, in both cases triangles are not possible."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.278,
            0.882,
            0.316
          ],
          "content": "**2. Can we say anything about the existence of a triangle for each of the following sets of lengths?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.324,
            0.169,
            0.34
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.36,
            0.448,
            0.378
          ],
          "content": "**(a) 10 km, 10 km and 25 km**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.385,
            0.458,
            0.403
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** A triangle does not exist"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.428,
            0.458,
            0.445
          ],
          "content": "**(b) 5 mm, 10 mm and 20 mm**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.453,
            0.458,
            0.471
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** A triangle does not exist"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.496,
            0.44,
            0.514
          ],
          "content": "**(c) 12 cm, 20 cm and 40 cm**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.52,
            0.458,
            0.539
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** A triangle does not exist"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.562,
            0.883,
            0.62
          ],
          "content": "**3. Will this always happen? That is, for any set of lengths, will there be at least two comparisons where the direct length is less than the sum of the other two? Explore for different sets of lengths.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.622,
            0.488,
            0.64
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** Some sets are 7, 10, 15; 12, 14, 18"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.675,
            0.251,
            0.693
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Page No. 156"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.705,
            0.299,
            0.724
          ],
          "content": "？ **Figure it out**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.735,
            0.882,
            0.793
          ],
          "content": "**1. Which of the following lengths can be the sidelengths of a triangle? Explain your answers. Note that for each set, the three lengths have the same unit of measure.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.129,
            0.8,
            0.181,
            0.817
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.828,
            0.266,
            0.846
          ],
          "content": "**(a) 2, 2, 5**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.857,
            0.363,
            0.873
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** Since 2 + 2 < 5."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.21,
            0.879,
            0.666,
            0.899
          ],
          "content": "So, these are not the side lengths of a triangle."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.493,
            0.928,
            0.507,
            0.941
          ],
          "content": "2"
        }
      ]
    }
